  "id": "COMPOUND:42902 - PROTEIN:6020",
  "verbalization": "Taxifolin 3-O-beta-D-xylopyranoside appears to have a shared target with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Taxifolin 3-O-beta-D-xylopyranoside to Guanylate cyclase soluble subunit alpha-2, which is then targeted by Isovitexin 2''-O-(6'''-(E)-p-coumaroyl)glucoside, ultimately targeting CDC2L1. The second and third pathways connect Taxifolin 3-O-beta-D-xylopyranoside to Tyrosine--tRNA ligase, which is targeted by Acetamide and Methylmalonic Acid, both of which also target CDC2L1. These pathways suggest a potential mechanism where Taxifolin 3-O-beta-D-xylopyranoside may influence cellular processes through intermediaries that modulate the activity of CDC2L1. The evidence supports a possible role for Taxifolin 3-O-beta-D-xylopyranoside in regulating the activity of PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
